## Request

Build the smallest complete release-reporter and instance-health slice on the existing hosted
dashboard. Report only locally known controlled facts, preserve independent instance authority,
make source and freshness explicit, and render unknown or divergent states honestly.

## Contract Decisions

- Health fields are controlled codes, versions, UTC timestamps, digests, and bounded counts.
- Reporter freshness, quiescence, and delivery state remain distinct.
- Installed, latest-known-stable, candidate/pending, and production-verified releases are separate
  concepts and each names its source and observation time.
- A semantic digest detects differing accepted lifecycle snapshots while excluding heartbeat-only
  changes; the server never merges rows to manufacture consensus.
- Canonical lookup failure and absent evidence render as unknown, never current by assumption.
- The hosted dashboard remains authenticated, advisory, read-only, and unable to mutate instances.

